iconv: add EBCDIC codepages IBM037, IBM500, IBM1140, IBM273

libxml2's encoding sniffer (xmlDetectEBCDIC) unconditionally opens an
IBM037 iconv handler to read the encoding declaration of any
EBCDIC-detected document, so without IBM037 *every* EBCDIC XML document
fails with "Unsupported encoding" even when the declared codepage (e.g.
the already-supported IBM1047) is available.  gcc 16's libgcobol codepage
layer (charmaps.cc) likewise resolves EBCDIC CODEPAGE names through
iconv_open.

Add the four pages relevant to us as pure data in codepages.h, following
the in-tree ibm1047 entry (same elided-quad packing; no code changes):

  IBM037   EBCDIC US/CA/NL/WT  - required by libxml2's sniffer
  IBM500   EBCDIC International (ebcdic-cp-ch: Swiss variant alias)
  IBM1140  IBM037 + euro at 0x9F
  IBM273   EBCDIC Germany/Austria

Tables generated from python's cp037/cp500/cp1140/cp273 codecs,
cross-checked byte-for-byte against glibc iconv; the one disagreement
(IBM273 0xBC: U+203E vs U+00AF) follows glibc (MACRON).  Both directions
work via the existing generic map paths.  Adds 1415 bytes to charmaps[].

